{"name":"Almost Charcoal","hex":"#6b7070","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"almost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Very close to, but not quite.","Up to, except for a negligible set (where negligible is not universally but contextually defined)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something or someone that doesn't quite make it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/almost"},{"term":"charcoal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["impure carbon obtained by destructive distillation of wood or other organic matter, that is, heating it in the absence of oxygen.","A stick of black carbon material used for drawing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark gray colour.","Made of charcoal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charcoal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Almost","blocks":[{"text":"In set theory, when dealing with sets of infinite size, the term almost or nearly is used to refer to all but a negligible amount of elements in the set. The notion of \"negligible\" depends on the context, and may mean \"of measure zero\", \"finite\", or \"countable\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almost","wikidata":"Q840148"},{"title":"Charcoal","blocks":[{"text":"Charcoal is a lightweight black residue made of carbon that is produced by strongly heating wood in minimal oxygen to remove all water and volatile constituents. In the traditional version of this pyrolysis process, called charcoal burning, often by forming a charcoal kiln, the heat is supplied by burning part of the starting material itself, with a limited supply of oxygen. The material can also be heated in a closed retort. Modern charcoal briquettes used for outdoor cooking may contain many other additives, e.g. coal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Charcoal_8.jpg/330px-Charcoal_8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charcoal","wikidata":"Q177463"},{"title":"Shades of gray","blocks":[{"text":"Variations of gray or grey include achromatic grayscale shades, which lie exactly between white and black, and nearby colors with low colorfulness. A selection of a number of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Shades_of_Gray.svg/330px-Shades_of_Gray.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_gray","wikidata":"Q3958716"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Charcoal_Packaging_-_Namibia.jpg/500px-Charcoal_Packaging_-_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Charcoal_Packaging_-_Namibia.jpg/1280px-Charcoal_Packaging_-_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Charcoal_Packaging_-_Namibia.jpg/500px-Charcoal_Packaging_-_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Packaging of charcoal for export in Namibia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharcoal_Packaging_-_Namibia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Charcoal_Kiln.JPG/500px-Charcoal_Kiln.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Charcoal_Kiln.JPG/1280px-Charcoal_Kiln.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Charcoal_Kiln.JPG/500px-Charcoal_Kiln.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An abandoned charcoal kiln near Walker, Arizona, US","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharcoal_Kiln.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikime